# The tables the AWS scripts load, tier and maintain (LAKE_TABLES_FILE). One line per table, whitespace-separated:
#   table      <domain>/<table folder>: the target is s3://LAKE_BUCKET/LAKE_PREFIX/<domain>/<table>/
#   kind       the entity kind the table holds (lake build --kind; the data-load signal names it)
#   pack       the pack folder (relative to the repository or the loader image): layout, promoted columns, id field
#   connector  the pack's Delta connector the table is for (one per source system)
#   landing    the dump prefix in s3://LANDING_BUCKET/, {date} replaced by the business date (YYYY-MM-DD)
#   date       the business-date field of each document, or - for "the day being loaded" (lake build --as-of)
#   partition  partition columns after business_date (lake build --partition-by), or - for none
#
# table                  kind    pack                   connector       landing                 date   partition
trading/trade_endur      trade   config/packs/trading   trade-endur     {date}/endur/           -      PRODUCT_TYPE
trading/trade_calypso    trade   config/packs/trading   trade-calypso   {date}/calypso/         -      PRODUCT_TYPE
trading/trade_murex      trade   config/packs/trading   trade-murex     {date}/murex/           -      PRODUCT_TYPE
